<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57289" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κητ-ώεις</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εσσα</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εν</span>, Homeric epith. of Lacedaemon, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοίλη Λακεδαίμων κητώεσσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.581
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.1
			</span></i>; perh.<i>full of hollows</i> or <i>ravines</i>,
			variously expld. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.5.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>, etc.; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καιετάεσσα</span>.
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> in later 
				Ep.
			, <i>cavernous</i>, of the wooden horse, <i><span class="en">
				Q.S.
				12.314
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κήτειος, πώεα</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
				<u>D.</u>
				43.251
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλαγξ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.274
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
